# GPS Configuration
# Raspberry Pi GPS Server Endpoint
# The app will try to use Raspberry Pi GPS first, then fallback to mobile GPS
VITE_GPS_PI_ENDPOINT=http://commutai.local:5000/api/gps

# Use Raspberry Pi GPS (true/false)
# Set to false to use only mobile GPS
VITE_USE_PI_GPS=true

Setup Instructions
Raspberry Pi GPS Server Setup:
Install dependencies on Pi:


bash
ssh chichi@commutai.local
sudo apt update
sudo apt install python3-pip python3-flask python3-flask-cors python3-serial
pip3 install flask flask-cors pyserial
Enable serial port:


bash
sudo raspi-config
# Interface Options -> Serial Port -> Enable serial port hardware
Copy and run the GPS server:


bash
# Copy the script to your Pi
scp raspberry-pi/gps_server.py chichi@commutai.local:~/gps_server.py
 
# Test it
python3 ~/gps_server.py
Set up as system service (optional, for auto-start):


bash
sudo systemctl enable commutai-gps.service
sudo systemctl start commutai-gps.service
App Configuration:
Create or update your .env file:



env
VITE_GPS_PI_ENDPOINT=http://commutai.local:5000/api/gps
VITE_USE_PI_GPS=true

